    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0678" n="580" xml:id="pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">031.11 American Museum of Natural History (4th
                    Asiatic)/92</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="12" xml:id="d649-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-01">May 1, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the course of a conversation today with the Minister for Foreign Affairs, the
                    latter volunteered the information that everything had been settled in
                    connection with the expedition of Dr. Roy Chapman Andrews. He said that he was
                    writing a formal letter concerning this matter very shortly. He said that
                    everything was now settled.</p>
                <p>I told him I was very glad to hear this and I would telegraph this information to
                    Dr. Andrews who was very anxious to hear about the matter.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d649-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d649-f1" n="12" type="source" xml:id="d649-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department without covering despatch; received June 19,
                    1930.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d649-f2" n="13" xml:id="d649-f2-content">
                <p>The expedition to Mongolia in the summer of 1930 was the last one, for permission
                    was not granted again in 1931 and further attempts were abandoned in 1932.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
